editor-terminal includes terminal screen algorithms adapted from Alacritty.

Upstream project: https://github.com/alacritty/alacritty
Source package: alacritty_terminal 0.26.0
Source commit: 94e7c8874e526b1e67b349d9ba30ddf81669119e
Published archive SHA-256:
bda177466b9524d59f1b12f0dd30b68696788e9992a7e959021c4a0ed96fcf59
Original package authors: Christian Duerr, Joe Wilm, and Alacritty contributors.
These portions retain Apache-2.0; the full license is LICENSE-ALACRITTY.

Integrated portions: typed cell coordinates; styled cells; screen and scrollback
storage/reflow; ANSI/VT screen operations; selection; wrapped Unicode regex search;
Vi cursor motion; and the associated algorithm and recorded-stream regressions.

Nanobug modifications:
- Integrate these algorithms into editor-terminal's private screen, grid,
  coordinates, selection and vi modules under its single Engine owner.
- Separate the ANSI handler, test support and regressions by responsibility.
- Keep snapshot serialization unconditional and retain the existing serialized
  cell fields, anonymous hyperlink identifiers and DA2 compatibility response.
- Return host effects through editor-terminal's events model; do not import the
  upstream PTY, process/event loop, thread, synchronization or platform code.
- Reduce the view projection to cursor/selection values needed by native drawing;
  process shutdown remains with the host rather than an upstream terminal entry point.
- Clearing an empty viewport adds no synthetic history row; occupied rows and styled
  spaces still retain their original scrollback behavior.
- Followed viewports reuse spare rows after logical reflow so restored first-line
  content remains visible without moving manually scrolled or alternate screens.

The upstream package, Cargo manifests, feature matrix, release documentation and
separate library entry point are not included. Nanobug does not depend on or
re-export alacritty_terminal. Focused VT byte decoding uses the vte dependency.
